    {
      "title": "Super Troopers 3",
      "distributor": "Searchlight Pictures",
      "theaters": 2760,
      "confidence": "high",
      "momentum": "softening",
      "rtCritic": 33,
      "metacritic": null,
      "rangeLow": 3700000,
      "rangeHigh": 4200000,
      "analysis": "Friday actuals confirm the pessimistic read: $1.7M from 2,760 theaters for a fourth-place finish, tracking to a $3.9M-$4M weekend per Deadline/Forbes — right at Box Office Theory's $3.5M pinpoint and well under Box Office Pro's original $6M-$9M long-range call. Reviews landed at 33% on Rotten Tomatoes, a new low for the franchise (below both Super Troopers' 37% and Super Troopers 2's 35%). That's a steep fall from Super Troopers 2's $15.1M opening ($30.6M total) — closer to Jackass: Best and Last's $8.4M-scale disappointment than any Scary Movie-style comeback. Ice Cream Man and Teenage Sex and Death at Camp Miasma also opened into the same crowded Friday.",
